\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Teamsters to Vote on Amazon Union Efforts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Noam Scheiber \par \uc2 605 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Delegates will vote on a resolution pledging ''all resources necessary'' for efforts to unionize the retail giant.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , which represents over one million workers in North America in industries including parcel delivery and freight, will vote on whether to make it a priority to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers and help them win a union contract.\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Amazon\uc2  is changing the nature of work in our country and touches many core Teamster industries and employers,'' states the resolution, which will be voted on at the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  convention on Thursday. The company ''presents an existential threat to the standards we have set in these industries,'' it says.\par \par \uc2 The resolution states that the union will ''supply all resources necessary'' and will eventually create an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  division to help organize workers at the company.\par \par \uc2 It does not elaborate on the timing for such a division or how much money or manpower the union will devote to the effort, and a union spokeswoman did not respond to a request for comment on those particulars. Last year the union had revenue of more than $200 million, according to Labor Department filings.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  did not immediately reply to a request for comment on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In an opinion column this month for Salon, Randy Korgan, a \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  official from Southern California who has been the national director for Amazon since the position was created last year, wrote that the union would bypass traditional workplace elections conducted by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Instead, Mr. Korgan wrote, the union will focus on building support from both \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers and from other warehouse and delivery workers and community members, and it aims to bring the company to the bargaining table by orchestrating strikes, boycotts, protests and other actions.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  defeated a conventional campaign organized by a retail workers union at a warehouse in Bessemer, Ala., this year, after which a number of union leaders suggested that a shift to the strategies highlighted by Mr. Korgan might be more fruitful. Those union leaders pointed out that federal labor law gives employers large advantages during election campaigns -- allowing companies to hold mandatory anti-union meetings, for example -- and that the government cannot fine employers who violate the law. (The retail workers union is challenging the results of the election at the Bessemer warehouse, accusing \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of intimidating workers.)\par \par \uc2 Support for the approach is far from unanimous within the labor movement, however.\par \par \uc2 In an interview after the election in Alabama, \uc2 Stuart Appelbaum\uc2 , the head of the retail workers union that oversaw the campaign, said seeking to win union elections at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses should remain a focus. ''If you want to build real power, you have to do it with a majority of workers,'' Mr. Appelbaum said at the time.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  holds its convention every five years and uses it to set the priorities that the union will pursue until the next convention. The resolution states that momentum for the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  campaign has been building since the union's last convention in 2016.\par \par \uc2 During that time, it says, various Teamster departments ''have been tracking \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's growth, presence and impact on Teamster industries and speaking with thousands of workers to develop different operating theories on the best way to engage and support \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers.''\par \par \uc2 A vote on whether to unionize at an Alabama warehouse failed earlier this year. The Teamsters plan to bring the company to the bargaining table by orchestrating strikes, protests and other actions. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Patrick T. Fallon/Agence France-Presse -- Getty Images FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210623eh6n00050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
