\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael M. Grynbaum and The Associated Press \par \uc2 494 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Banking\par \par \uc2 Biden to Repeal Changes To Discrimination Law\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration said on Tuesday that it would repeal changes made by the Trump administration to a law made to stop banks from discriminating against racial minorities and the poor.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Office of the Comptroller of the Currency\uc2  said it planned to reconsider regulations it wrote in 2020 governing the law, the Community Reinvestment Act, requiring banks to document how well they are lending to communities that surround their branches.\par \par \uc2 Former President Donald J. Trump's comptroller, \uc2 Joseph Otting\uc2 , made revising the law a priority. The law is widely respected by banks and activists, but both sides have agreed the law was out of date. Many banks operate entirely online and A.T.M.s are ubiquitous, making it increasingly more difficult to define what a ''community'' was.\par \par \uc2 But the changes last year were considered too broad for Democratic leaders. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Workplace\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  to Set A $25 Minimum Wage\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  plans to set the minimum wage for all positions at the company to $25 an hour by 2025.\par \par \uc2 It would be the highest minimum wage paid by a big bank and could pressure rivals to follow suit. Wages have been rising at major banks in recent years amid pressure from outside groups to address wealth inequality.\par \par \uc2 The bank will also mandate that vendors it does business with pay their employees at least $15 an hour. The bank says 99 percent of its vendors are already in compliance at that level.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  raised its minimum wage to $15 an hour in 2017, to $17 an hour in 2019, and to $20 an hour last year, all under the chief executive, \uc2 Brian Moynihan\uc2 . The bank has more than 210,000 employees.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have pushed increasing the minimum wage across all industries for several years. President Biden campaigned on raising the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour from its current level, $7.25. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Aviation\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers Seek Records On Two \uc2 Boeing Aircraft\par \par \uc2 Two key members of Congress are seeking records from \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2  about production problems with two of the company's most popular airliners. The lawmakers are focusing on the Boeing 737 Max and a larger plane, the 787, which \uc2 Boeing\uc2  calls the Dreamliner.\par \par \uc2 House Transportation Committee chairman, \uc2 Peter DeFazio\uc2 , Democrat of Oregon, said on Tuesday that there were ''new and ongoing issues that point to problems in maintaining quality control and appropriate F.A.A. oversight of production issues.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeFazio was joined in the records request by \uc2 Rick Larsen\uc2 , Democrat of Washington and chairman of the House aviation subcommittee. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said it was reviewing the request. The F.A.A. did not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 About 100 Max jets were idled in April because of improper electrical wiring that affected cockpit instruments. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY MIKE BLAKE/REUTERS) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210519eh5j00051\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
